are exactly $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-1,1].$" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515916 1072 #uuid "0611bd23-ee0e-588d-8010-4f01ff7ae188" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515916 1074 "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm\\pi,\\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515917 1080 "false" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515917 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515917 1083 #uuid "0f0a2436-d2b8-5ada-bc74-03b482439509" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515918 1080 "false" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515918 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515918 1083 #uuid "0fe3f231-f5ba-5be1-be9e-5913a0ba515b" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515915 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515986 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515919 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515919 1077 "III" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515919 1078 #edb/ref 17592186515986 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515919 1079 #uuid "11def7b4-86ae-5083-b3a6-95ac3f063630" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515920 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515948 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515920 1075 #edb/ref 17592