ref 17592186045485 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515955 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zeros of the function are exactly $x=n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The vertical asymptotes are exactly $x=2n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The range of the function is $(0,\\infty).$" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515955 1072 #uuid "7bf14e5f-b763-51cd-9bef-9f8efe8615bd" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515955 1074 "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm\\pi,\\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515956 1080 "true" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515956 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515956 1083 #uuid "861fc676-efd2-540d-b645-1548f6595165" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515957 1080 "true" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515957 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515957 1083 #uuid "887815d4-2bcf-5d8b-9e5f-f7ea52b630ba" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515958 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515936 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515958 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516004 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515958 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186515958 1077 "II" 13194139535555 17592186045443 true] [17592186